  "articleBody": "Choosing a new bathroom countertop can feel like a big decision, right? There are so many options out there! First, you'll want to think about what really matters to you: is it super durability, easy cleaning, or a specific look? Different materials, like quartz or granite, offer various benefits. You'll also need to consider your budget and how much wear and tear the countertop will get. For instance, a guest bathroom might not need the same hardy material as a busy family bathroom. When you're talking with installers, don't be shy about asking if they handle both the fabrication and installation, what the finished cost covers, and what kind of care the material will need after it’s installed. It's smart to ask for examples of their work or even see samples so you can get a real feel for it. And remember, sometimes those tricky jobs with undermount sinks or custom cuts are best left to the pros. If you're ready to explore your options and get some expert advice, HH Remodeling is here to help you find that perfect fit for your Denver area home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}